OL,3,AWhat can I do to protect myself after
OL,4,A'Asos hacked' message?
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf a strange-looking message from Asos
OL,7,Fpopped up on your phone on Tuesday, you
OL,8,Fmay be worrying what it could mean and
OL,9,Fwhether you need to do anything.
OL,11,FThe online retailer has emailed
OL,12,Fcustomers apologising for the
OL,13,F"unauthorised push notification"
OL,14,Fcontaining an external link, adding
OL,15,Fthat they should disregard the message
OL,16,Fand not click on it.
OL,18,FHere's what has happened, and what
OL,19,Fthose who may have been affected are
OL,20,Fbeing advised to do.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
FL,116,105,200,300,0,100
